sequenceDiagram
  participant O as BoardActor (fence 7)
  participant PG as Postgres
  O->>PG: BEGIN
  O->>PG: SELECT op_id, version FROM<br/>board_ops WHERE op_id =<br/>ANY(batch)
  Note over O: ops already stored are<br/>duplicates: answer with<br/>their stored version
  O->>PG: UPDATE boards SET version =<br/>version + n WHERE id = ? AND<br/>fence = 7 RETURNING version
  alt zero rows
    PG-->>O: nothing
    Note over O: board row gone = deleted<br/>(amendment 27), otherwise<br/>fenced out: NOT_OWNER, close
  else version v
    O->>PG: INSERT n ops with versions<br/>v-n+1 .. v
    O->>PG: COMMIT (only if the 2 s<br/>budget is not spent)
    PG-->>O: ok
    Note over O: now apply to memory,<br/>remember in LRU, ACK,<br/>publish
  end
